flowchart TD
    OC["OpenClaw"]
    P1["Profile: agent1"]
    P2["Profile: agent2"]
    S1["Session 1"]
    S2["Session 2"]
    SYS["System message"]
    USR["User message"]
    AI["AI message"]
    CALL["Tool call: goal — { create, objective, acceptance_criteria }"]
    TOOLS["Tools: goal · read · write"]
    INFER["★ AUTO-INFERRED — in the main session\nThe agent itself, in the same turn as the user message,\ninfers the goal and declares it with this call.\nNo background API call infers the goal."]
    JUDGE["Judge (auxiliary model) — checks DONE only\njudge_goal asks only 'is the goal DONE?' — it never infers the goal."]
    INJ["What injects the goal back into the session?\n1 · Heartbeat tick — next_continuation_prompt feeds the goal back as a user-role message.\n2 · Idle-wake — the barrier-wake chore re-pokes an active goal after 15 min idle (idle_wake_seconds = 900).\nBoth re-assert the EXISTING goal. Never inferred in the background."]
    OVER["Side note — /goal is an override, not the flow\nDen can set the goal with /goal — a user-set goal always wins,\nthe agent cannot replace it. That is an override, not the flow."]
    WATCH["WATCH OUT — known bugs in Hermes (do not copy)\nGoal dies at context compression — flat goal:<session_id> lookup, no parent walk.\nAgent goals have no per-turn judge or turn budget — no stall detection.\nA dead judge never pauses the goal — it fails open to continue.\nThe agent grades its own criteria — it writes them, the audit checks them.\nStop-check plugin broken on Linux — symlink to a macOS path, does not load.\nGoal tool off by default — the mechanism is silent unless opted in."]

